     "text": "Internal forces (folding, faulting, volcanism, earthquakes) build landforms; external forces (weathering, erosion, deposition) wear them down. The atmosphere has four layers. Weather is short-term; climate is the long-term average, controlled by latitude, altitude, the sea, clouds and currents. Ethiopia has five agro-climatic zones."
